course: dictionary
lesson: 3088
title: Abbreviations in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer word. Writers shorten long words so they are quicker to write, and readers use the context to work out what the short form stands for. «Our hearts and brains work with electric signals that doctors measure with an ECG and an EEG.» The words around EEG tell you it is something doctors measure in the body.
explain: The clues are electric signals, brains and doctors measure. Ask yourself: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence? EEG is a noun, so you can write «an EEG» or «EEGs».
explain: Science texts use many abbreviations, so it helps to learn the common ones. When the context is not enough, a dictionary settles it: EEG is short for electroencephalogram, a long word that is much harder to read and spell.
fact: EEG is short for electroencephalogram.
fact: An EEG is a medical test that records the electrical activity of the brain as wavy lines.
fact: The word EEG can also mean the machine that does this test.
fact: Doctors use an EEG to study sleep and conditions such as epilepsy.
fact: In an EEG test, small metal discs are put on the head.
exercise: What does EEG stand for? | Electric eel group | Electrocardiogram | *Electroencephalogram | Easy exercise game
exercise: «Doctors measure with an ECG and an EEG.» What do doctors do with an EEG? | Bake a cake | Count the birds in the park | Paint pictures of the sea | *Measure electrical activity in the brain
exercise: What does an EEG show? | *Wavy lines of brain activity | Pictures of food | Maps of the moon | Loud noises
test: Which of these is the abbreviation for electroencephalogram? | Brain | *EEG | Test | Electric
test: Why do doctors use an EEG? | To go shopping | To make bread | To measure how tall you are | *To study sleep and conditions such as epilepsy
exam: Based on «doctors measure with an ECG and an EEG», what can you tell about an EEG? | A country in Europe | A kind of food | A colour of paint | *A way of measuring something in the body
